# What docker builds never need from the repo's top folder. The cloud server's image builds from it, and so does any
# image when Docker has no BuildKit, which ignores the images' own lists (raspberry_pi/*/Dockerfile.dockerignore).
# It keeps the build quick, and your keys and data out of what's sent to Docker.
**/.env
config/settings.local.yaml
raspberry_pi/mine
data
models
certs
.git
.venv
.worktrees
.superpowers
.pytest_cache
_screenshots
benchmarks
docs
tests
dev_ui
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
